# Normalize ALL text files to LF, in git and in the working tree, on every
# platform regardless of core.autocrlf. Global autocrlf=true plus PowerShell/tool
# whole-file writes otherwise reintroduce CRLF, which MUSTER's review/integration
# gates flag as defects - stalling the auto loop on a self-inflicted wound.
# The eol=lf attribute overrides core.autocrlf, including muster's own
# -c core.autocrlf=false commits, so the clean filter always stores LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git Bash sh chokes on CRLF line endings (bad shebang, ${var%x} artifacts, etc).
# Pin the sh engine scripts to LF regardless of platform autocrlf settings, so
# a fresh clone/checkout on Windows (the normal muster:init install path)
# doesn't silently break the sh engine.
*.sh text eol=lf
